&lt;p&gt;This is a unique opportunity to shape the future Treasury technology landscape within a global organisation, driving strategic change while delivering tangible business value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience implementing, managing, or supporting Treasury Management Systems within a corporate or financial services environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of UK and international treasury operations, including cash management, liquidity, financial instruments, and regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated project management expertise, with a track record of delivering complex transformation and systems initiatives on time and within budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced analytical skills, including strong proficiency in Excel, reporting tools, and data-driven decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating treasury platforms with ERPs, banking systems, and payment networks is highly advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive problem solver with a strong focus on process optimisation, controls, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to influence and collaborate effectively at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working both independently and as part of a global, fast-paced team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An appreciation of emerging technologies, including the application of AI to enhance treasury operations, insights, and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
